From 766b8ef5ccb7c0c9bf4350a123d03a3af1182d36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leandro Berto <leandroberto2010@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:45:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] recomp: lift-time relocation of fixed guest arrays
 (--relocate)

A title's fixed-size BSS arrays cannot grow in place: the next global
follows. Every access goes through a constant, though, so the lift can
move one: immediates and displacements inside [lo, hi) become
to + (v - lo); with "base", register-relative offsets into a fixed object
too (never immediates: those overlap code addresses; never jmp/call
operands: jump tables); with "size", a cmp against the old end becomes the
new end (loop sentinels). Rewrites are listed in relocate_sites.txt.

Runtime: g_xbox_image_extra reserves zeroed memory right after the image,
before the toolkit region, so the target address is fixed at lift time.
Zero keeps the old layout.

RECOMP_WATCH on POSIX hosts: print the guest call chain scanned off the
guest stack (as the Win32 path does) and the host pc on x86-64 Linux.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EEc1xt2bgZTWAVrjEf7eN6
